<section class="nit nit-faq nit-section" aria-labelledby="nit-faq-heading">
  <div class="nit-container nit-faq__inner">
    <div class="nit-faq__head"><p class="nit-label nit-reveal">Questions</p><h2 class="nit-h1 nit-faq__heading nit-reveal" id="nit-faq-heading">
        The things people ask
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="nit-faq__list" data-nit-stagger><details
            class="nit-faq__item nit-reveal"
            name="nit-faq-nit-faq"
            open
            
          >
            <summary class="nit-faq__summary">
              <h3 class="nit-faq__question">When will it arrive?</h3>
              <span class="nit-faq__marker"><svg
  class="nit-icon nit-icon--chevron"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="1.5"
  stroke-linecap="butt"
  stroke-linejoin="miter"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
><path d="m6.5 10 5.5 5 5.5-5"/></svg>
</span>
            </summary>

            <div class="nit-faq__answer nit-body nit-muted nit-measure">
              <p>Ordered before 2pm on a working day, it leaves the same day. After that, the next working day. Royal Mail Tracked 48 then takes two to three working days, occasionally four to the Highlands and Islands.</p><p>If it is out of stock the product page says so and will not take the order. We would rather lose the sale than take your money and email you a delay a week later.</p>
            </div>
          </details><details
            class="nit-faq__item nit-reveal"
            name="nit-faq-nit-faq"
            
            
          >
            <summary class="nit-faq__summary">
              <h3 class="nit-faq__question">Will it actually lift pet hair, or just move it around?</h3>
              <span class="nit-faq__marker"><svg
  class="nit-icon nit-icon--chevron"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="1.5"
  stroke-linecap="butt"
  stroke-linejoin="miter"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
><path d="m6.5 10 5.5 5 5.5-5"/></svg>
</span>
            </summary>

            <div class="nit-faq__answer nit-body nit-muted nit-measure">
              <p>Hair worked into a seat weave needs lift rather than sweep, which is what the 18,500 Pa and the brush head are for. It will clear dog hair from fabric seats and carpet mats in one or two passes.</p><p>What it will not do is beat a full-size upholstery machine on a heavily matted seat that has never been cleaned. Nothing at this size will.</p>
            </div>
          </details><details
            class="nit-faq__item nit-reveal"
            name="nit-faq-nit-faq"
            
            
          >
            <summary class="nit-faq__summary">
              <h3 class="nit-faq__question">How long does a charge last, and is that one car or two?</h3>
              <span class="nit-faq__marker"><svg
  class="nit-icon nit-icon--chevron"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="1.5"
  stroke-linecap="butt"
  stroke-linejoin="miter"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
><path d="m6.5 10 5.5 5 5.5-5"/></svg>
</span>
            </summary>

            <div class="nit-faq__answer nit-body nit-muted nit-measure">
              <p>Thirty-two minutes on a full charge. A single car interior &#8212; footwells, seats, boot and the console &#8212; takes about twelve to fifteen minutes at a normal pace, so one charge covers two cars with room to spare.</p><p>A full charge from empty takes about two and a half hours over USB-C.</p>
            </div>
          </details><details
            class="nit-faq__item nit-reveal"
            name="nit-faq-nit-faq"
            
            
          >
            <summary class="nit-faq__summary">
              <h3 class="nit-faq__question">Can I charge it in the car?</h3>
              <span class="nit-faq__marker"><svg
  class="nit-icon nit-icon--chevron"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="1.5"
  stroke-linecap="butt"
  stroke-linejoin="miter"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
><path d="m6.5 10 5.5 5 5.5-5"/></svg>
</span>
            </summary>

            <div class="nit-faq__answer nit-body nit-muted nit-measure">
              <p>Yes. It charges over USB-C from any 5V source, including a car adapter or a power bank. It will not run while charging from a car socket, because the draw while running is higher than a 12V adapter reliably supplies.</p>
            </div>
          </details><details
            class="nit-faq__item nit-reveal"
            name="nit-faq-nit-faq"
            
            
          >
            <summary class="nit-faq__summary">
              <h3 class="nit-faq__question">Do I have to keep buying filters?</h3>
              <span class="nit-faq__marker"><svg
  class="nit-icon nit-icon--chevron"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="1.5"
  stroke-linecap="butt"
  stroke-linejoin="miter"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
><path d="m6.5 10 5.5 5 5.5-5"/></svg>
</span>
            </summary>

            <div class="nit-faq__answer nit-body nit-muted nit-measure">
              <p>No. The HEPA filter washes under a tap and goes back in once it is completely dry. There is no cartridge and no subscription.</p><p>It is still a consumable &#8212; after a year or two of regular use it will stop recovering and want replacing. Spares are sold at cost.</p>
            </div>
          </details><details
            class="nit-faq__item nit-reveal"
            name="nit-faq-nit-faq"
            
            
          >
            <summary class="nit-faq__summary">
              <h3 class="nit-faq__question">How loud is it?</h3>
              <span class="nit-faq__marker"><svg
  class="nit-icon nit-icon--chevron"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="1.5"
  stroke-linecap="butt"
  stroke-linejoin="miter"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
><path d="m6.5 10 5.5 5 5.5-5"/></svg>
</span>
            </summary>

            <div class="nit-faq__answer nit-body nit-muted nit-measure">
              <p>72 dB at a metre, which is roughly a domestic vacuum and quieter than a forecourt machine. Loud enough that you would not use it at seven in the morning outside a neighbour's window, quiet enough to hold a conversation over.</p>
            </div>
          </details><details
            class="nit-faq__item nit-reveal"
            name="nit-faq-nit-faq"
            
            
          >
            <summary class="nit-faq__summary">
              <h3 class="nit-faq__question">Will it fit in the door pocket?</h3>
              <span class="nit-faq__marker"><svg
  class="nit-icon nit-icon--chevron"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="1.5"
  stroke-linecap="butt"
  stroke-linejoin="miter"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
><path d="m6.5 10 5.5 5 5.5-5"/></svg>
</span>
            </summary>

            <div class="nit-faq__answer nit-body nit-muted nit-measure">
              <p>310 &#215; 78 &#215; 90 mm and 680 g. It fits most door bins and every glovebox we have tried, and the case takes the nozzle and brush head alongside it in a boot side pocket.</p>
            </div>
          </details><details
            class="nit-faq__item nit-reveal"
            name="nit-faq-nit-faq"
            
            
          >
            <summary class="nit-faq__summary">
              <h3 class="nit-faq__question">Is it any good for wet mess?</h3>
              <span class="nit-faq__marker"><svg
  class="nit-icon nit-icon--chevron"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="1.5"
  stroke-linecap="butt"
  stroke-linejoin="miter"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
><path d="m6.5 10 5.5 5 5.5-5"/></svg>
</span>
            </summary>

            <div class="nit-faq__answer nit-body nit-muted nit-measure">
              <p>No, and using it for one will damage it. It is a dry vacuum: spilled coffee, wet mud and melted snow are all jobs for a cloth first. Let a wet patch dry fully before vacuuming it.</p>
            </div>
          </details><details
            class="nit-faq__item nit-reveal"
            name="nit-faq-nit-faq"
            
            
          >
            <summary class="nit-faq__summary">
              <h3 class="nit-faq__question">Can I use it for anything other than the car?</h3>
              <span class="nit-faq__marker"><svg
  class="nit-icon nit-icon--chevron"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="1.5"
  stroke-linecap="butt"
  stroke-linejoin="miter"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
><path d="m6.5 10 5.5 5 5.5-5"/></svg>
</span>
            </summary>

            <div class="nit-faq__answer nit-body nit-muted nit-measure">
              <p>People mostly do. Pushchairs, dog crates, the stairs, keyboards, the inside of a laptop bag, campervans and boats. It is built around car geometry rather than restricted to it.</p>
            </div>
          </details><details
            class="nit-faq__item nit-reveal"
            name="nit-faq-nit-faq"
            
            
          >
            <summary class="nit-faq__summary">
              <h3 class="nit-faq__question">What if it is not right for me?</h3>
              <span class="nit-faq__marker"><svg
  class="nit-icon nit-icon--chevron"
  width="20"
  height="20"
  viewBox="0 0 24 24"
  fill="none"
  stroke="currentColor"
  stroke-width="1.5"
  stroke-linecap="butt"
  stroke-linejoin="miter"
  aria-hidden="true"
  focusable="false"
><path d="m6.5 10 5.5 5 5.5-5"/></svg>
</span>
            </summary>

            <div class="nit-faq__answer nit-body nit-muted nit-measure">
              <p>Send it back within 30 days, used or unused, and we pay the return postage. There is no restocking fee and nothing to argue about &#8212; if it did not do what you hoped, that is a good enough reason.</p>
            </div>
          </details></div><div class="nit-small nit-muted nit-measure nit-faq__footer nit-reveal">
        <p>Not answered here? <a href="/pages/contact">Ask us</a> and the reply comes from a person in the UK, usually the same day.</p>
      </div></div>
</section>

